From c97aafdde2e10f3e1d1fc6589fda45c22bc20ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:20:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] render: load the shared atlas's static rows from their
 ASTC bake

With its run-time rows in a texture of their own (previous patch), the
shared atlas's static part takes no writes, so it can be ASTC 4x4: a byte
a texel instead of four. `--bake-atlas`, which the port's patcher runs,
already baked the whole atlas, but nothing could load it.

The bake now covers only the static rows, and is named by their size and
content key (HudAtlas::static_key, read while the packed pixels are still
in memory): before, its name was only the atlas's size, so a pack with
another atlas of that size would have loaded the wrong textures. Earlier
atlas bakes in the cache folder are deleted when a new one is written.

The renderer loads the bake when this GPU samples ASTC (the capability,
astc::supported) and the RGBA spill is there, then streams only the
dynamic rows from the spill; the log says which:
  shared atlas static rows 4096x2152 from their ASTC bake (8 MiB),
  dynamic rows 4096x2968 RGBA (46 MiB)
Without the bake or the capability nothing changes. The whole-atlas copy
for shader packs, pack text shaders and native mods reads the static rows
from that spill, since an ASTC texture copies into no RGBA one.

On the default resources the atlas then takes 55 MiB of GPU memory instead
of 80, and a launch reads 46 MiB of it from the card instead of 80. Text
from the bitmap fonts draws texel for texel as from RGBA; GUI sprites differ
in a few edge shades (checked on PC, Mesa's GL with ASTC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
